  "description": "FULL PLANNING PERMISSION FOR THE PROPOSED\r\nERECTION OF A NEW SHOPFRONT",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt;line-height:107%;\r\nfont-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Aptos;mso-fareast-theme-font:\r\nminor-latin;mso-ansi-language:EN-GB;mso-fareast-language:EN-US;mso-bidi-language:\r\nAR-SA&quot;&gt;The proposal fails to demonstrate a design-led response to the site and\r\nwould result in a shopfront and signage that are visually intrusive and\r\nunsympathetic to the architectural character of the locally listed building.\r\nThe proposal fails to conserve or enhance the significance of the heritage\r\nasset, introduces excessive and poorly integrated signage and does\r\nnot respond positively to local character or context. The proposal is contrary\r\nPolicies D12.3, D12.4, D12.5 and D12.7, and the Council’s adopted Shopfront\r\nDesign Guidance (2017).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
